      "parent_index": null,
      "last_updated": "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Profiles",
      "order": 2,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "Temperature against conductivity separates the four habitats almost on its own: groundwater is thermally buffered and carbonate-rich, riverwater is cold and oxygen-saturated, hyporheic sediment is the most conductive and nearly anoxic, and soil is the coldest and least mineralised. Nitrate against dissolved organic carbon shows the same split from the other side.",
      "wf_tag": "nextflow/ampliseq"
    },
